      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T08:19:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, I looked into this a bit more and I don\u0027t see clean and sensible way to verify this. I know it\u0027s just GATT, but what we really want here is to check if HAP connected as a service. So after encryption, Android discovers services, connects HAP, reads presets. And here is the problem: just in this test, PTS doesn\u0027t send back preset list, but error, like so:\n\n```\n07-24 07:27:13.786  1002  3934  3967 D HapClientNativeInterface: onPresetInfoError: HearingAccessStackEvent {type:EVENT_TYPE_ON_PRESET_INFO_ERROR, device: XX:XX:XX:XX:17:01, value1: {statusCode: STATUS_OPERATION_NOT_POSSIBLE}, value2: {presetIndex: 1}, value3: {groupId: 0}, list: {list: empty}}\n```\n\nand this leads to disconnection. If PTS would send back presets, we would have confirmation that HAP characteristics are there. I see that there\u0027s similar MMI in VCP, and although I don\u0027t like it, we probably can just return \u0027OK\u0027 here, as we do there.\n\nI think it\u0027s not that big of a deal, because in other tests presets are received okay, and that means Android correctly discovers characteristics and caches handles.",
